---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Principles | Macro Evidence"
  description="The engineering and governance principles Macro Evidence uses to make rigor concrete in the work."
>
  <PageIntro
    kicker="How we work"
    title="Discipline is part of the infrastructure."
    lead="We use explicit engineering and governance requirements so rigor shows up in the work itself. These are design standards and decision constraints, not claims that every current implementation is complete."
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="site-container">
      <div class="definition-grid">
        <article class="definition-card">
          <h2 class="micro-label">01 / Provenance</h2>
          <span class="question">Where did it come from?</span>
          <p>
            Source identity and lineage should remain represented or documented
            to the depth the system actually implements. Provenance is a
            traceability requirement, not a claim of exhaustive end-to-end
            lineage.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="definition-card">
          <h2 class="micro-label">02 / Validation</h2>
          <span class="question">What rules did it pass?</span>
          <p>
            Data should be checked against documented rules before it is
            accepted. The scope of those checks should remain explicit rather
            than being inflated into broader statistical or methodological
            assurance.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="definition-card">
          <h2 class="micro-label">03 / Reproducibility</h2>
          <span class="question">Can it be recreated?</span>
          <p>
            Pipelines, configuration, and transformation logic should make
            results recreatable from the same source data or equivalent inputs
            without undocumented manual judgment.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="definition-card">
          <h2 class="micro-label">04 / Maintainability</h2>
          <span class="question">Can it evolve without hidden context?</span>
          <p>
            Systems and documentation should remain understandable enough to
            change deliberately rather than depending on undocumented
            institutional knowledge or one-off conventions.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="definition-card">
          <h2 class="micro-label">05 / Transparent limitations</h2>
          <span class="question">What is not being claimed?</span>
          <p>
            Relevant methodology, decisions, and material limitations should be
            stated plainly while preserving legitimate private, operational, and
            security boundaries.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="definition-card">
          <h2 class="micro-label">06 / Auditability</h2>
          <span class="question">What can another person inspect?</span>
          <p>
            Evidence, records, decisions, and relevant system context should
            support systematic review to the depth actually implemented without
            implying certification, assurance, or guaranteed correctness.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section relationship-section">
    <div class="site-container split">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Why it matters</span>
        <h2>Evidence should remain open to scrutiny.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="reading">
        <p>
          Macro Evidence publishes relevant public records and engineering
          context so scrutiny is possible. Those records support review; the
          person evaluating the evidence still decides what to trust.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
